// =============================================================================
// MemQL Agent Reference (RETIRED)
// =============================================================================
//
// The `agent X { ... }` DSL primitive this file used to document has been
// REMOVED. Platform agents are now declared as `seed X { ... }` declarations
// targeting the v1:agents:agent concept; the SeedMaterializer
// (component/memql/seed_materializer.go) materializes one v1:agents:agent
// row per user (perUser scope) or one global row (global scope) at engine
// startup + on user-create events.
//
// See:
//   - dsl/agents/plannerAgent.memql         -- seed example (global scope)
//   - dsl/agents/trainerAgent.memql         -- seed example (global scope)
//   - dsl/agents/builtins.memql             -- the agent(name, args) builtin
//                                              (KEPT; the runtime invocation
//                                              surface stays as-is)
//   - component/memql/seed_parser.go        -- the seed parser
//   - component/memql/seed_materializer.go  -- row materialization
//   - component/memql/agents.go             -- AgentRegistry (row-backed)
//
// The per-user assistant seed (once dsl/agents/assistant.memql) was deleted
// from this repo -- it now ships in the product DSL bundle
// (MEMQL_DSL_PATH), not the engine tree. The two seeds above are the only
// seed examples that remain in-repo.
//
// This file is kept (under the underscore-prefix skip rule the loader
// honors) so a search for "agent reference" lands on the migration breadcrumb
// rather than a 404. The historical content lives in git history.
